WEBVTT

00:02.319 --> 00:04.819
[SlGHS]

00:10.761 --> 00:12.361
CHARLlE: Morning.
- Mm.

00:12.362 --> 00:14.862
Morning.

00:15.399 --> 00:18.033
Charlie, please don't start anything.

00:18.034 --> 00:21.094
Too late. I woke up started.

00:22.706 --> 00:26.164
- I have to get to work.
- Okay.

00:26.343 --> 00:28.843
I've got a job for you.

00:28.945 --> 00:31.445
We'll finish this tonight.

00:32.015 --> 00:34.650
I may have to finish this myself.

00:34.651 --> 00:36.085
Knock yourself out.

00:36.086 --> 00:39.288
It's no fun if you have permission.

00:39.289 --> 00:43.092
CHELSEA: So, Charlie, I was thinking maybe
tonight we could stay at my place.

00:43.093 --> 00:46.324
Oh, no, no, no.

00:46.496 --> 00:50.065
CHELSEA: Charlie?
- I'm sorry, did you say something?

00:50.066 --> 00:52.735
CHELSEA: I said, maybe tonight we could
stay at my place.

00:52.736 --> 00:55.236
You wanna play on my face?

00:56.973 --> 00:59.473
Stay at my place.

00:59.509 --> 01:01.811
Oh.

01:01.812 --> 01:04.613
- What about it?
- I've been coming here for three weeks...

01:04.614 --> 01:07.550
...and it's like an hour drive
for me to get to work.

01:07.551 --> 01:11.221
Well, I'd be happy to spring for a cab.

01:11.354 --> 01:13.956
- It's not the drive.
- You just said it was the drive.

01:13.957 --> 01:16.258
What I mean is
if we're gonna see each other...

01:16.259 --> 01:19.595
...on a regular basis,
there should be some give and take.

01:19.596 --> 01:20.863
Based on last night...

01:20.864 --> 01:24.900
...we're pretty even-steven
in the give-and-take department.

01:24.901 --> 01:29.004
And if I recall correctly,
you're up one take.

01:29.005 --> 01:33.735
Hey, of the two us,
I'm the one with tennis elbow.

01:34.644 --> 01:36.345
CHELSEA:
So, what about tonight?

01:36.346 --> 01:37.546
[SlGHS]

01:37.547 --> 01:40.015
I'd love to,
but it might be a little tricky.

01:40.016 --> 01:41.851
CHELSEA:
Why?

01:41.852 --> 01:44.353
[WHlSPERlNG]
Oh, I knew she'd ask me that.

01:44.354 --> 01:48.023
CHELSEA: I'm starting to get the feeling
that you only wanna see me at your place...

01:48.024 --> 01:49.925
...and at your convenience.

01:49.926 --> 01:53.054
No, of course not.

01:53.797 --> 01:56.899
Well then, fine.
You'll stay at my place tonight.

01:56.900 --> 02:00.130
Sounds great. Looking forward to it.

02:11.648 --> 02:13.549
So, what do you wanna do
this weekend?

02:13.550 --> 02:18.680
Doesn't matter, just as long
as you and I are together.

02:20.390 --> 02:22.625
What did you do?

02:31.868 --> 02:33.802
Do I need to call your mother and ask?

02:33.803 --> 02:36.939
If you want,
but you know how she pushes your buttons.

02:36.940 --> 02:41.090
- I'll take that chance.
- Fine, I don't care.

02:42.379 --> 02:45.014
All right, All right.
I got thrown off the school bus.

02:45.015 --> 02:48.185
You got the spine of a gummy bear.

02:50.153 --> 02:52.054
Why were you thrown off the bus?

02:52.055 --> 02:54.523
Well, actually, it's a funny story.

02:54.524 --> 02:55.958
Amuse me.

02:55.959 --> 02:59.595
Have you ever heard of this thing
called mooning?

02:59.596 --> 03:01.597
Yeah. Yeah, it rings a bell.

03:01.598 --> 03:03.599
The bus was going past
the girls' track team.

03:03.600 --> 03:05.701
A bunch of us thought
it'd be funny to moon them.

03:05.702 --> 03:08.137
[CHUCKLES]

03:08.138 --> 03:10.239
See? She gets it.

03:10.240 --> 03:14.176
- Berta.
- Sorry. I'm just remembering my prom.

03:14.177 --> 03:15.377
[SlGHS]

03:15.378 --> 03:16.579
So, what happened?

03:16.580 --> 03:20.716
Well, I was working near the high school
that night and I thought it would be fun...

03:20.717 --> 03:24.019
- ...to drive the backhoe--
- Not you.

03:24.020 --> 03:27.820
- Him.
- Well, excuse me for sharing.

03:29.059 --> 03:33.762
- What happened?
- Well, it sounds like Berta had quite a prom.

03:33.763 --> 03:35.731
You're skating on thin ice, Jake.

03:35.732 --> 03:37.866
Boy, something we haven't done
in a long time...

03:37.867 --> 03:39.835
- ...skating.
- Jake.

03:39.836 --> 03:41.804
Mom grounded me for two weeks.

03:41.805 --> 03:45.574
- Why didn't your mother tell me about this?
- I promised I'd tell you.

03:45.575 --> 03:48.535
What can I say? She believed me.

03:48.912 --> 03:51.180
So, how about a movie?
Little father-son bonding?

03:51.181 --> 03:52.748
No, no. No movies.

03:52.749 --> 03:54.149
- Skating?
- No skating.

03:54.150 --> 03:56.318
- Fine.
- Also, uh, no TV...

03:56.319 --> 03:58.821
...no video games,
no cell phones, and no iPods.

03:58.822 --> 04:01.290
Nothing that gives you
any amusement or enjoyment.

04:01.291 --> 04:06.711
- Couldn't you just smack me with a belt?
- Get out of here.

04:08.465 --> 04:10.965
I'm bored.

04:14.904 --> 04:17.654
- Oh, man.
- What's the matter?

04:17.741 --> 04:22.611
Did you know that Culver City
is all the way down near the airport?

04:22.612 --> 04:24.380
Yes.

04:24.381 --> 04:27.016
That's gotta be like 45 minutes
from here.

04:27.017 --> 04:30.087
- lf there's no traffic.
- Traffic?

04:31.421 --> 04:34.491
Is this Culver City place popular?

04:35.191 --> 04:36.392
Not particularly.

04:36.393 --> 04:41.563
But there are other people with cars, living
lives completely separate from your own.

04:41.564 --> 04:44.394
Oh, right. I hate those people.

04:45.201 --> 04:48.971
"So, what's in Culver City? " he asked,
knowing the only possible answer.

04:48.972 --> 04:51.840
Can you believe she wants me to schlep
over to her place...

04:51.841 --> 04:54.710
...just so we can spend
the night together?

04:54.711 --> 05:00.211
Oh, you poor guy.
You have to drive 45 minutes to get laid.

05:01.885 --> 05:04.395
And 45 minutes to get back.

05:06.423 --> 05:10.893
That's 90 minutes behind the wheel
for 20, 30 minutes behind--

05:10.894 --> 05:13.696
Well, I don't need to draw you a map.

05:13.697 --> 05:15.497
You're breaking my heart.

05:15.498 --> 05:17.099
And it's not just that.

05:17.100 --> 05:21.770
She said there's only street parking,
which means trees.

05:21.771 --> 05:25.074
And trees have that, you know,
toxic syrup that drips out of them...

05:25.075 --> 05:27.509
...and gets all over your car.

05:27.510 --> 05:30.760
- Sap.
- lf I make that drive, I am.

05:32.515 --> 05:35.751
Wait a minute. You said it was better to go
to the woman's house...

05:35.752 --> 05:40.122
- ...so that you could make a quick getaway.
- Yeah, for one-nighters that's fine.

05:40.123 --> 05:42.024
But this girl, I care about her.

05:42.025 --> 05:44.727
We've been seeing each other
for almost a month.

05:44.728 --> 05:47.963
And yet you just found out
where she lives.

05:47.964 --> 05:52.334
There's a difference
between caring and stalking, Alan.

05:52.335 --> 05:54.703
- Hey, Dad, I need my laptop.
- What for?

05:54.704 --> 05:56.605
- Homework.
- What homework?

05:56.606 --> 05:59.473
Um-- Damn, you're good.

06:04.147 --> 06:06.582
Thanks for driving all the way
over here, Charlie.

06:06.583 --> 06:10.486
Are you kidding?
I would have walked here if I had to.

06:10.487 --> 06:13.889
Probably would have been faster
with the traffic.

06:13.890 --> 06:15.958
Good night.

06:15.959 --> 06:18.459
Good night.

06:22.999 --> 06:25.499
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

06:31.040 --> 06:34.243
- What are you doing?
- I heard a car door.

06:34.244 --> 06:36.311
Your Mercedes is fine, Charlie.

06:36.312 --> 06:39.672
I know, I know. Just double checking.

06:39.716 --> 06:42.216
[CAR ALARM BEEPS]

06:43.653 --> 06:46.622
Probably gonna get sap
all over the car cover.

06:46.623 --> 06:52.143
- lsn't that what it's for?
- You don't get it. That's fine.

06:54.264 --> 06:57.533
- No TV in the bedroom, huh?
- It's in the living room.

06:57.534 --> 07:01.069
- So you just got the one?
- How many do I need?

07:01.070 --> 07:05.007
Well, you've got three rooms
and a bath, so...

07:05.008 --> 07:06.542
...four.

07:06.543 --> 07:11.513
If you wanna go watch television
instead of cuddling, that's up to you.

07:11.514 --> 07:14.483
No, no, I'd much rather cuddle.

07:17.187 --> 07:19.421
At my house, we could do both.

07:19.422 --> 07:22.653
You know, cuddling and SportsCenter.

07:22.826 --> 07:26.086
- Good night, Charlie.
- Sweet dreams.

07:44.781 --> 07:46.448
[SlGHS]

07:46.449 --> 07:48.617
What now?

07:48.618 --> 07:52.387
Nothing. I'm just used to sleeping
on the other side of the bed.

07:52.388 --> 07:53.922
Yeah, so?

07:53.923 --> 07:56.592
So I usually sleep on my left side...

07:56.593 --> 07:59.595
...which faces me towards
the edge of the mattress.

07:59.596 --> 08:03.532
But here, I'm facing the back of your head,
which is fine.

08:03.533 --> 08:08.637
There are certainly times
when I enjoy seeing it from that angle.

08:08.638 --> 08:13.609
But, you know, when I'm trying to sleep,
it's a little disconcerting.

08:13.610 --> 08:17.070
Well, I'm sorry, but this is my side.

08:17.247 --> 08:20.315
But you sleep on the other side
at my house.

08:20.316 --> 08:22.918
Because it's your house.
This is my house.

08:22.919 --> 08:25.520
- But I'm a guest.
- And I'm a guest at your house.

08:25.521 --> 08:27.789
- That's different.
- How?

08:27.790 --> 08:31.470
- Give me a minute.
- Good night, Charlie.

08:32.262 --> 08:35.789
Boy, you're being pretty inflexible.

08:35.965 --> 08:38.166
Oh, you think I'm inflexible.

08:38.167 --> 08:40.667
Well, not physically.

08:41.337 --> 08:46.708
But you gotta admit, in this regard,
you're a little stubborn.

08:46.709 --> 08:49.644
Good night, Charlie.

08:53.016 --> 08:55.746
Okay. Good night.

08:59.155 --> 09:00.589
How about this?

09:00.590 --> 09:01.790
[CHELSEA SCOFFS]

09:01.791 --> 09:05.928
If we switch sides and an armed intruder
came in, I could leap up and protect you.

09:05.929 --> 09:10.332
But this way, you're pretty much
guaranteed to catch the first bullet.

09:10.333 --> 09:13.613
What if he comes through the window?

09:15.838 --> 09:17.673
Oh, great.

09:17.674 --> 09:20.844
Now, I'm never gonna get to sleep.

09:30.386 --> 09:32.220
[MUSlC PLAYlNG ON TV]

09:32.221 --> 09:34.721
ALAN:
Jake?

09:39.162 --> 09:41.912
You better not be watching TV.

09:56.646 --> 09:59.146
[ALAN SCOFFS]

10:01.517 --> 10:04.782
Ah. Maybe he's upstairs.

10:05.254 --> 10:07.754
[FOOTSTEPS]

10:08.358 --> 10:10.858
[DOOR CLlCKlNG]

10:12.061 --> 10:14.561
JAKE:
Uh-oh.

10:19.435 --> 10:21.935
[WATER DRlPPlNG]

10:28.578 --> 10:31.078
[DOG BARKlNG]

10:33.583 --> 10:36.083
[SlGHS]

10:38.588 --> 10:41.023
[CAR ENGlNE REVS]

10:41.024 --> 10:43.524
[SlGHS]

10:49.465 --> 10:51.965
[CHELSEA MOANS]

10:55.571 --> 11:00.121
It's like trying to sleep
in the freaking jungle.

11:11.554 --> 11:14.894
[CAT CATERWAULS
THEN CHARLlE SCREAMS]

11:17.160 --> 11:19.594
- What's going on?
- Nothing. Nothing.

11:19.595 --> 11:24.132
I was going to the bathroom
and I stepped on a cat.

11:24.133 --> 11:27.169
You don't have to sneak out.
If you wanna leave, leave.

11:27.170 --> 11:31.807
Whoa, I'd say someone woke up
on the wrong side of the bed.

11:31.808 --> 11:34.810
But I don't wanna revisit that topic.

11:34.811 --> 11:37.311
Goodbye, Charlie.

11:37.613 --> 11:40.283
Gee, you sound kind of angry.

11:40.483 --> 11:42.184
Why would I be angry?

11:42.185 --> 11:45.287
Just because I drive to Malibu
every night for a month...

11:45.288 --> 11:47.656
...and you won't stay
even one night with me?

11:47.657 --> 11:52.561
Well, that. And, you know,
possibly crippling your cat.

11:52.562 --> 11:55.297
- Go home, Charlie.
- Are you sure?

11:55.298 --> 11:57.532
I'm begging you.

11:57.533 --> 12:00.627
Okay, if that's what you want.

12:04.841 --> 12:07.341
So tomorrow at my place?

12:13.249 --> 12:18.219
You make love like a woman,
but you throw like a man.

12:39.542 --> 12:41.576
ALAN:
Jake?

12:41.577 --> 12:42.777
[SHOUTS]

12:42.778 --> 12:45.013
[SEAGULL SQUAWKS]

12:45.014 --> 12:46.815
Why are you sleeping out here?

12:46.816 --> 12:48.783
I was, um...

12:48.784 --> 12:51.284
...camping?

12:52.221 --> 12:56.531
Okay, well, as long
as you're not watching TV.

13:00.229 --> 13:02.729
Oh.

13:03.499 --> 13:06.024
Stupid birds.

13:06.202 --> 13:08.803
Hey, how'd it go last night?

13:08.804 --> 13:12.874
I couldn't do it, Alan.
I tried, but I couldn't.

13:12.875 --> 13:15.477
Oh, well, that happens
to all men occasionally.

13:15.478 --> 13:17.679
Especially when you get to be our age.

13:17.680 --> 13:20.180
What are you talking about?

13:20.850 --> 13:23.285
- What are you talking about?
- I'm talking about...

13:23.286 --> 13:27.556
...how I'm so set in my ways, I couldn't
spend one night in a strange house.

13:27.557 --> 13:30.759
Yeah, that's what I'm talking about.

13:30.760 --> 13:33.328
There was a time
when I could sleep anywhere.

13:33.329 --> 13:38.066
Couches, floors, witness boxes,
police cars, jail cells.

13:38.067 --> 13:40.969
That's not sleeping, that's passing out.

13:40.970 --> 13:44.540
I'm not gonna argue semantics with you.

13:44.774 --> 13:48.443
The point is,
I was really uncomfortable over there.

13:48.444 --> 13:51.546
Even if I got to sleep,
the morning would have been a disaster.

13:51.547 --> 13:54.243
- How so?
- Think about it.

13:54.417 --> 13:58.253
After I had my morning coffee,
where would I go to do my business?

13:58.254 --> 13:59.688
ALAN:
Oh, right.

13:59.689 --> 14:03.058
You always wanna have
home-field advantage for that.

14:03.059 --> 14:06.595
She's got one of those
wooden toilet seats.

14:06.596 --> 14:11.146
It'd have been like sitting
on Pinocchio's mouth.

14:12.602 --> 14:16.571
Ever wonder about people
who can poop in a gas station?

14:16.572 --> 14:18.607
I mean, what is wrong with them?

14:18.608 --> 14:20.408
And what about Porta Potties?

14:20.409 --> 14:23.812
Ugh, those aren't people, those are animals.

14:23.813 --> 14:26.414
I'd rather go in the trunk of my car.

14:26.415 --> 14:28.915
I have.

14:30.653 --> 14:33.121
You've gone in the trunk of your car?
Ha, ha.

14:33.122 --> 14:35.622
No, yours.

14:39.629 --> 14:42.129
That was you?

14:44.467 --> 14:48.887
I convinced myself
a coyote had gotten in there.

14:51.307 --> 14:56.547
[PLAYlNG DEEP PURPLE'S "SMOKE
ON THE WATER" ON THE PlANO]

15:07.256 --> 15:09.846
What the hell are you doing?

15:10.059 --> 15:11.559
Playing "Smoke on the Water."

15:11.560 --> 15:14.950
- With your tongue?
- Pretty cool, huh?

15:14.964 --> 15:18.566
No, it's not cool. It's disgusting.
Alan, get in here.

15:18.567 --> 15:20.268
What now?

15:20.269 --> 15:22.859
Your kid's licking my piano.

15:23.806 --> 15:26.875
Jake, don't lick your uncle's piano.

15:26.876 --> 15:29.110
- I'm bored.
- Well, go read a book.

15:29.111 --> 15:33.761
- I don't wanna read a book.
- Then go lick a book.

15:35.418 --> 15:38.119
How long is this whole grounding thing
gonna go on for?

15:38.120 --> 15:40.188
- Two weeks.
- Two weeks?

15:40.189 --> 15:43.658
He stuck his ass out a bus window
at the girls' track team.

15:43.659 --> 15:45.960
That's what you're punishing him for?

15:45.961 --> 15:49.731
When you were his age,
you mooned the girls' choir.

15:49.732 --> 15:54.903
No, uh, when I was his age,
you pantsed me in front of the girls' choir.

15:54.904 --> 15:59.694
Oh, right. Well, either way,
you made the year book.

16:01.010 --> 16:03.278
- Berta, I'm leaving.
BERTA: Hang on.

16:03.279 --> 16:04.679
Where you going?

16:04.680 --> 16:08.650
I talked Chelsea into giving me another
chance to spend the night at her place.

16:08.651 --> 16:11.151
Here's your overnight bag.

16:12.088 --> 16:14.055
- Thank you.
- All that's for one night?

16:14.056 --> 16:19.276
One night and one morning
business meeting with Pinocchio.

16:20.830 --> 16:22.897
You got your flip-flops for the shower...

16:22.898 --> 16:25.266
...your bath towel, hand towel
and washcloth...

16:25.267 --> 16:27.869
- ...your hand soap, face soap and shampoo.
- Great.

16:27.870 --> 16:32.474
One handheld TV, your goose-down pillow,
Egyptian-cotton pillowcase and sheets...

16:32.475 --> 16:35.343
...and a Ziploc baggie
of your special French-roast coffee.

16:35.344 --> 16:38.380
- Terrific.
- One jar of seedless raspberry jam...

16:38.381 --> 16:44.711
...a mild laxative, and one roll of quilted
toilet paper with lanolin.

16:45.254 --> 16:46.621
Okay.

16:46.622 --> 16:47.822
[GRUNTS]

16:47.823 --> 16:50.553
Culver City, here I come.

16:55.197 --> 16:58.897
- He ain't gonna make it.
- Not a chance.

16:59.568 --> 17:03.071
You know, I have never once
seen him eat seedless raspberry jam.

17:03.072 --> 17:09.452
That's because you've never applied
a thin layer to your hindquarters.

17:14.283 --> 17:17.152
CHELSEA: I'm so glad you decided
this was important to you, Charlie.

17:17.153 --> 17:20.179
Well, you're important to me.

17:21.056 --> 17:23.158
What are you doing?

17:23.159 --> 17:25.659
I brought my sheets.

17:25.761 --> 17:28.511
You wanna grab the other side?

17:28.798 --> 17:33.435
- What's wrong with my sheets?
- Nothing, nothing. But mine are better.

17:33.436 --> 17:37.916
Egyptian cotton.
Like, eight-million thread count.

17:38.174 --> 17:42.610
And good news. I solved
the "wrong side of the bed" situation.

17:42.611 --> 17:44.379
Okay.

17:44.380 --> 17:48.080
I'll just sleep with my head down there.

17:48.951 --> 17:51.586
That way I'm facing the right way.

17:51.587 --> 17:53.788
But then your feet will be in my face.

17:53.789 --> 17:57.549
Way ahead of you.
Peppermint foot lotion.

17:58.327 --> 18:01.996
You'll think you're sleeping
in Candy Land.

18:01.997 --> 18:04.497
Oh, before I forget.

18:05.301 --> 18:08.136
- Toilet paper?
- Don't get your hopes up...

18:08.137 --> 18:11.177
...but I'm gonna make the effort.

18:14.910 --> 18:17.410
ALAN:
Hey, Jake?

18:18.447 --> 18:20.947
You out here?

18:23.118 --> 18:25.618
Seen my kid?

18:33.796 --> 18:37.163
[CARS RAClNG ON TV]

18:41.170 --> 18:45.106
- What the hell?
- Can I have some privacy, please?

18:45.107 --> 18:47.308
No--

18:47.309 --> 18:50.778
- Get out of the tub. Out of the tub.
- Fine.

18:50.779 --> 18:53.615
You're unbelievable.
Is TV really that important to you?

18:53.616 --> 18:56.116
Do you really have to ask?

18:56.552 --> 18:58.586
- Go to your room.
- Okay. But check out...

18:58.587 --> 19:01.089
...Uncle Charlie's toilet seat. It heats up.

19:01.090 --> 19:03.590
Just go.

19:05.094 --> 19:09.063
JAKE: Can I have this raspberry jam?
- Don't touch the jam.

19:09.064 --> 19:11.564
[SlGHS]

19:18.774 --> 19:21.274
Oh.

19:22.344 --> 19:24.844
Toasty.

19:27.917 --> 19:30.717
If only I could poop at night.

19:32.288 --> 19:35.248
Maybe I'll just pee girly style.

19:47.770 --> 19:50.270
- Charlie.
- Aah!

19:53.242 --> 19:55.610
- What?
- This isn't working for me.

19:55.611 --> 19:58.111
My feet too minty?

19:58.447 --> 19:59.714
It's not your feet.

19:59.715 --> 20:02.250
Well, it is your feet,
but it's also the sheets...

20:02.251 --> 20:05.620
...the pillows, the towels, the TV,
the electric toothbrush.

20:05.621 --> 20:09.424
It's not a toothbrush.
It's an ultrasonic dental appliance.

20:09.425 --> 20:15.363
